# Server analytics (PostHog)

Server events go through `captureServerEvent` in `src/lib/analytics.ts` (`server-only`).

```ts
captureServerEvent("help_center_submitted", {
  distinctId: user.id,
  properties: { email, message, accountEmail },
});
```

- Pass the **unprefixed** event name. The helper adds `NEXT_PUBLIC_EVENT_PREFIX`.
- One `posthog-node` client per warm instance (`flushAt: 1`, `flushInterval: 0`). The helper schedules `after(() => flushWithTimeout())`, and falls back to `waitUntil` from `@vercel/functions` when `after` throws (no Next.js request scope).
- Serverless freezes the instance when the response is sent. `after` / `waitUntil` keep the invocation alive until the flush settles. The handler returns without waiting. `flushWithTimeout` races the flush against ~2.5s and logs errors instead of rejecting.
- Record the product action once. A signup or a help submission is one event, including when the handler runs several database queries.
- `Analytics.track` / `identify` use the same client and the same scheduled flush.

